The `find_valid_string` function splits the string into chunks of three characters each (or fewer if the string length is not divisible by three). It then filters out chunks that do not contain any vowels. The remaining chunks are sorted by the number of vowels (in descending order), length (in ascending order), and lexicographically (in ascending order). The first chunk in this sorted list is returned as the result.

The `solution` function ties everything together by calling `remove_symbols` and `find_valid_string` in sequence.

This solution has a time complexity of O(n), where n is the length of the input string, because each character in the string is processed a constant number of times.

