The time complexity of this algorithm is O(n), as it performs a single pass through the array to partition it and then another pass to find the median. The space complexity is O(1), as it only uses a constant amount of extra space for the pivot index and temporary variables.

Note that this implementation assumes the input array is sorted. If the input array is unsorted, you would first need to sort it before applying this algorithm. Sorting the array would increase the time complexity to O(n log n).

