The `count_substring_occurrences` function repeatedly calls `boyer_moore` to find the next occurrence of the substring in the text, updating the `text` to search in the remaining part after each occurrence. It keeps a count of the occurrences and returns this count once no more occurrences are found.

The time complexity of this function is O(n), where n is the length of the text, due to the nature of the Boyer-Moore algorithm. The space complexity is O(m), where m is the length of the substring, due to the storage of the bad character and good suffix tables.

